(1089841, 131712, 25787, '<td valign="top">Nice photo.  Where were you in the pet challenge.</td>', 'Nice photo.  Where were you in the pet challenge.', '2005-01-03 23:08:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(1089843, 131566, 28261, '<td valign="top">It is hard to say if the dirt these guys are throwing up is distracting or if there is a color cast/over saturation problem here.  To begin with, this is a great stop-action capture!  Almost every dog is in focus and yet the foreground (rabbit) is slightly blurred which means you chose just the right dog to focus on.  Your crop choice is great, leading the eye from top right to left to bottom as the race is leading the viewer.  Your border choice is not annoying or overpowering and the shot''s color scheme combined with it give a 50''s feel to the composition.<br/> <br/>Unfortunately, I see nothing candid in this entry.  Yes, candid can be used with animals, but this is a sporting event (I won''t get political on this one), and the shot is stop action, emotion: excitement, anticpation.  I commend your composition as technically high, deduct for what seems to be a bluish/neon color cast and cannot find the link to the challenge.  This leaves this entry at a 3.</td>', 'It is hard to say if the dirt these guys are throwing up is distracting or if there is a color cast/over saturation problem here.  To begin with, this is a great stop-action capture!  Almost every dog is in focus and yet the foreground (rabbit) is slightly blurred which means you chose just the right dog to focus on.  Your crop choice is great, leading the eye from top right to left to bottom as the race is leading the viewer.  Your border choice is not annoying or overpowering and the shot''s color scheme combined with it give a 50''s feel to the composition. Unfortunately, I see nothing candid in this entry.  Yes, candid can be used with animals, but this is a sporting event (I won''t get political on this one), and the shot is stop action, emotion: excitement, anticpation.  I commend your composition as technically high, deduct for what seems to be a bluish/neon color cast and cannot find the link to the challenge.  This leaves this entry at a 3.', '2005-01-03 23:10:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(1089852, 132522, 28261, '<td valign="top">Candid, yes most likely, could be staged, lighting on magazine is not too blown out, but the rest of the shot is so darn black as to not be able to make out anything but the form of the profile, the hands and the mag.  This setup could be seen as very artistic and I give high points for what it could be, but find the magazine to be the main subject, the candid human, to be underexposed so much as to bas9ically not be present and the mag is too out of focus to leave an impact.  Rating: 2</td>', 'Candid, yes most likely, could be staged, lighting on magazine is not too blown out, but the rest of the shot is so darn black as to not be able to make out anything but the form of the profile, the hands and the mag.  This setup could be seen as very artistic and I give high points for what it could be, but find the magazine to be the main subject, the candid human, to be underexposed so much as to bas9ically not be present and the mag is too out of focus to leave an impact.  Rating: 2', '2005-01-03 23:13:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(1089858, 132821, 28261, '<td valign="top">While this is a great and I do mean "Holy Cow Batman look at all those fireworks!", I cannot see any link to the challenge of candid here.  Aside from the spectacular wow look at all those freakin fireworks factor, the crop is the only other thing going for this shot in the candid challenge and it is only enough to rate a 3.</td>', 'While this is a great and I do mean "Holy Cow Batman look at all those fireworks!", I cannot see any link to the challenge of candid here.  Aside from the spectacular wow look at all those freakin fireworks factor, the crop is the only other thing going for this shot in the candid challenge and it is only enough to rate a 3.', '2005-01-03 23:16:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(1089867, 132200, 28261, '<td valign="top">Reminds me of Rocky Horror.  Does not say candid to me, although I can see how someone might consider this candid and I''ll give half credit.<br/> <br/>  What this image really says is Blurry, OverExposed Lamps, Camera Shake, Snapshot just to get an entry.<br/> <br/>This type of shot would need a tripod, not a stabilizing wall or chair.  Without a specific target for evaluation in the crowd, I can only say this image rates a two.</td>', 'Reminds me of Rocky Horror.  Does not say candid to me, although I can see how someone might consider this candid and I''ll give half credit.   What this image really says is Blurry, OverExposed Lamps, Camera Shake, Snapshot just to get an entry. This type of shot would need a tripod, not a stabilizing wall or chair.  Without a specific target for evaluation in the crowd, I can only say this image rates a two.', '2005-01-03 23:19:50.000000', NULL, 1),
